# Showcase — 20-bar A-minor piece written to demonstrate what deck can actually
# do on GBA hardware, while still being worth listening to on its own.
#
# The arrangement is NOT written into the notes. Every track plays its full
# length; what you hear is the intensifier gating stems in and out while one
# playhead keeps running. Captured with intensity automated 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 1
# at four-bar boundaries, so the piece assembles itself and then strips back:
#
#   bars  0-3   int 0   bass + pad                  (the bed)
#   bars  4-7   int 1   + plucked theme + arp       (the tune arrives)
#   bars  8-11  int 2   + kick + hats               (the groove locks in)
#   bars 12-15  int 3   + stabs, theme an octave up (peak; E major for lift)
#   bars 16-19  int 1   drums and stabs drop out    (the comedown)
#
# Progression is i-VI-III-VII in A minor (Am F C G), turning to Am F C E at the
# peak — the E major borrows a G# from the harmonic minor, which is where the
# lift at bar 15 comes from, then Am F G Am to land.
#
# Voices, and the hardware each one costs:
#   Pluck  wave ch3    named wavetable + ADSR       (the hero voice)
#   Pad    pulse ch1   duty 50, vibrato
#   Arp    pulse ch2   duty 25, hardware arpeggio
#   Hats   noise ch4   short-mode LFSR
#   Bass   PCM         sine, so the wave channel stays free for the pluck
#   Kick   PCM         pitch_drop transient
#   Stab   PCM         bitcrushed saw
#
# 2 pulse / 1 wave / 1 noise are exactly the LR35902 caps; 3 PCM voices sit
# inside the 6-voice music budget.
deck 1
bpm 150

# Odd harmonics only — no 2nd, 4th or 6th. That hollow, clarinet-like spectrum
# is what makes a plucked string read as plucked; the ADSR below supplies the
# attack and decay that `fx reverb_send` would have on a host, since fx is a
# hard bake error here.
wave nylon harmonics 1 0 0.4 0 0.2 0 0.1

track Bass id bass gen gbaDirectSound layer 0 * 20
  gen waveform sine vol 13
  adsr a 0.004 d 0.25 s 12 r 0.08
  # S1 — sparse, one root per bar with an octave lift into the next
  note 45 0 3 v 104
  note 57 3 1 v 88
  note 41 4 3 v 104
  note 53 7 1 v 88
  note 36 8 3 v 104
  note 48 11 1 v 88
  note 43 12 3 v 106
  note 55 15 1 v 92
  # S2 — quarters
  note 45 16 1 v 110
  note 45 17 1 v 92
  note 57 18 1 v 102
  note 45 19 1 v 94
  note 41 20 1 v 110
  note 41 21 1 v 92
  note 53 22 1 v 102
  note 41 23 1 v 94
